## 5. TESTING & QUALITY

### Build Validation

```bash
# Always test build before committing major changes
npm run build

# Check for:
# ✓ TypeScript errors
# ✓ ESLint warnings
# ✓ Build time (should be < 5s for incremental)
```

### Code Quality Checklist

Before committing:
- [ ] Build succeeds without errors
- [ ] No TypeScript 'any' types introduced
- [ ] All imports use @ alias (not relative from root)
- [ ] German text for user-facing messages
- [ ] Error handling with user-friendly messages
- [ ] Non-blocking analytics where applicable
- [ ] Mobile-responsive design tested

---

## 6. DEPLOYMENT

### Production Build

```bash
# Local production build
npm run build
npm run start

# Deployment (Turso database + Vercel/similar)
# 1. Set environment variables
# 2. Run migrations: npx drizzle-kit push
# 3. Deploy with npm run build
```

### Database Migrations

```bash
# After schema changes in lib/schema.ts
npx drizzle-kit generate  # Generate migration
npx drizzle-kit push      # Apply to database
```

---

## 7. COMMON PITFALLS TO AVOID

### Frontend

❌ **Don't:** Use 'any' types
✅ **Do:** Define proper interfaces

❌ **Don't:** Create global components for feature-specific UI
✅ **Do:** Co-locate components in feature directories

❌ **Don't:** Inline 100+ lines of JSX in one component
✅ **Do:** Extract reusable components (aim for < 150 lines per component)

### Backend

❌ **Don't:** Let analytics errors break user flow
✅ **Do:** Wrap analytics in try-catch with non-blocking error logging

❌ **Don't:** Use string concatenation for SQL queries
✅ **Do:** Use Drizzle's query builder with parameterized queries

❌ **Don't:** Expose internal error details to users
✅ **Do:** Provide friendly German error messages

### Refactoring

❌ **Don't:** Refactor the entire codebase at once
✅ **Do:** Phase-by-phase with builds and commits after each phase

❌ **Don't:** Optimize prematurely
✅ **Do:** Focus on readability and maintainability first

---

## 8. USEFUL COMMANDS

```bash
# Development
npm run dev                          # Start dev server
npm run build                        # Production build
npm run lint                         # ESLint check

# Database
npx drizzle-kit studio              # Visual database explorer
npx drizzle-kit generate            # Generate migration
npx drizzle-kit push                # Apply schema changes

# Scripts (in /scripts directory)
npx tsx scripts/delete-all-files.ts # Clean up Gemini files
npx tsx scripts/migrate-configs-to-db.ts # Migrate configs
```

---

## Summary

This project follows a **simple, pragmatic approach**:
- Local state over complex state management
- Co-located components over premature abstraction
- Drizzle ORM over raw SQL
- Phase-by-phase refactoring over big rewrites
- User experience over technical perfection

When in doubt, **prefer simplicity and readability** over cleverness.
